A letter waits on your cot, folded small, in your brother's careful hand.
"Mother says to tell you the roof held through the storm, that we're proud of you, and that you should eat." # speaker: ulf
"Asa wants to know if you've seen Grandfather. She thinks he'll be at a long table with a horn of mead. I didn't tell her what he died of." # speaker: ulf
"Firewood is dear this winter. We'll manage." # speaker: ulf
* [Write back: "All is well here."]
  You leave out the queue, and the smell, and the man who wept on your table.
